From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tessera <tessera@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:25:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Document shared level root in runtime snapshots


diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/RuntimeWorldManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/RuntimeWorldManager.java
index 2a8405c47..366487960 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/RuntimeWorldManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/RuntimeWorldManager.java
@@ -68,6 +68,22 @@ public interface RuntimeWorldManager {
      * allowed; their data, statistics and advancements are flushed before the
      * snapshot is published below {@code players/}.</p>
      *
+     * <p>The required {@code level/} output contains the shared level root:
+     * {@code level.dat}, optional {@code level.dat_old}, {@code data/},
+     * {@code datapacks/}, optional {@code generated/} and {@code resourcepacks/},
+     * and safe regular root files. {@code session.lock}, {@code dimensions/},
+     * {@code players/}, links and special files are not copied into it.
+     * Missing {@code level.dat} fails the operation. All loaded worlds are
+     * temporarily frozen because level and player storage are shared.</p>
+     *
+     * <p>{@code level/}, {@code worlds/} and {@code players/} are staged together
+     * inside the same protected snapshot phase. Existing output children cause
+     * a collision before saving. Success is returned only after all three have
+     * been published; a publication failure rolls back outputs created by this
+     * invocation. Unrelated caller-owned children remain untouched. Readers
+     * must wait for the returned result: publication consists of three directory
+     * moves, not a crash-atomic filesystem transaction.</p>
+     *
      * <p>This method does not use the immutable-template cache used by
      * {@link #cloneWorldAsync(World, NamespacedKey, WorldCloneOptions)}. Every
      * invocation saves and copies a new state. The operation is asynchronous
